Z||000033||erikred||11-08-2001||09:39 AM||||What about a Pontiac SD? They can put out close to 400hp without the turbo or NOS. It would be a hell of alot easier swap too. You can buy a complete race engine for &lt;$6000 or build a new one from KRP for about $5000. Stroke it to 3.0l and put on a good turbo setup, 400hp should not be a problem, even with the pushrod heads! By the time you figure in the huge amount of engineering and extra cost to install the ricer motors you may be ahead to just drop in the SD. BTW, there are still tons of parts available for this engine.<P>Erik-||||reg||12
